s": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le16ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: Wow. Amy. You're taking a lot of stuff to Africa. You may have been right Peter, the difference between men and women is luggage.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>:  Peter! You said that? You can be so insensitive. You could at least think about other people's feelings once.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>:  Could you not be so judgemental all the time? Must you always talk like that?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: Alright! Alright. You two are adorable. You might have gotten me once, but unlike some people I know, you can't fool me twice. Why so much stuff?", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>:  Because I'm going with her on her spectacular getaway to Africa.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: What?  You might have let me know!\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: We are telling you now.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: How? You couldn't have had enough time.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: We talked to Candice about it. She said whereas last time I was extremely busy, this time will be more supervisory in nature, so I'll have more free time than on my last trip.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: What about tickets?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: There were plenty of seats and even though we won't be sitting together, we're booked on the same flight.", "id": 2, "time": "32500"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: What about a visa?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: Americans might have needed a visa in the past, but now you don't if you are staying less than 90 days.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: And vaccinations?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: Lesotho might have had a yellow fever problem before, but now it's safe.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: It seems much more convenient than last time.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: A little bit.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: Well, we are heading to the airport now. We don't want to be held up in traffic.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: Send me a postcard? Would that be too much to ask?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: No problem. Do you want to share a cab?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>:  No thanks.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: Bye. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: Bye.", "id": 3, "time": "62000"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: Are you as excited as I am?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: I'm super excited.\nOh wait. I'm going into O'Malley's to say hello to someone. I'll be right back.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Amy</span>: You may do as you please.", "id": 4, "time": "104000"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: Hey, John.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">John</span>:   Peter. Hey! Is Vanessa with you?\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: Uh. Sadly, no. My girlfriend and I are traipsing off to Africa.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">John</span>:  Africa. Wow. Good for you.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Peter</span>: I just wanted to say hello and wish you luck.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">John</span>: Thank you Peter. You too.<br>", "id": 5, "time": "119000"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob11re2img04.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">John</span>:   Well, John. As you've made your bed, you might as well lie in it.\n</br><span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Vanessa</span>: Ready to roll the dice just one more time?", "id": 6, "time": "144500"}]}}], "_data": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "I have researched the trip. Would it be too much to ask you to book the tickets? Also, you might have let me know that you asked your mother to come. You could have asked me first. Now, we will have to supervise her and make sure she doesn't wander. You couldn't have thought very carefully. I think we might have to get a fourth ticket. If your mother is coming, I am asking my aunt to come.  That way, they can spend some time together and try to have an amazing holiday."}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "All's Well That Ends Well", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Final Goodbyes", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "PlaceholderUnderstands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbial Clauses: Concession/Contrast and Comparison", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Let's review the different ways you can add diversity in the way you speak and write. You can use adverbial clauses to add detail to your descriptions of people, events and things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">You use <span class=\"underline\">concession or contrast clauses</span> to express an idea that suggests the opposite of the main part of the sentence. They are useful in both writing and speaking since they make your language more dynamic and diverse. You introduce concession or contrast clauses with conjunctions like <span class=\"italic\">although</span>, <span class=\"italic\">though</span>, <span class=\"italic\">even though</span>, <span class=\"italic\">whereas</span>, <span class=\"italic\">while</span> and <span class=\"italic\">even if</span>. </li></ol>For example: <span class=\"italic\"></br><span class=\"strong\"> Whereas </span>last time our schedule was quite busy, this time it will be much easier.</span></br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">  Even though</span> we won't be sitting together, we are booked on the same flights.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">You can use adverbial <span class=\"underline\">clauses of comparison to describe manner</span> (the way in which someone does something). You introduce the comparative clause with the relative adverb <span class=\"italic\">as</span>.  </li></ol>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">  As </span>you've made your bed, you might as well lie in it. </span> This expression means that if you make a decision, you will have to accept the consequences.</br><span class=\"italic\"> It ended <span class=\"strong\">as </span>I expected.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"3\">You can use adverbial <span class=\"underline\">clauses of comparison to describe degree</span> (when you want to say how much more something or someone is compared to something or someone else). You introduce adverbial clauses of comparison of degree with the subordinating conjunction <span class=\"italic\">than</span>, or by the relative adverb <span class=\"italic\">as</span>. </li></ol>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I will have more free time<span class=\"strong\"> than</span> on my last trip.</span>  </br><span class=\"italic\"> Are you <span class=\"strong\">as</span> excited <span class=\"strong\">as </span> I am?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I will have more free time <span class=\"strong\">than </span>on my last trip. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you <span class=\"strong\">as</span> excited <span class=\"strong\">as</span>  I am?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " It seems much more convenient<span class=\"strong\"> than</span> last time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You may do <span class=\"strong\">as </span>you please.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Whereas</span> last time I was extremely busy, this time will be more supervisory in nature.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals to Express Annoyance in the Present and in the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals in their present and past forms to express annoyance about a situation or to make a critical comment.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to express annoyance and criticism about the past, you can use modals such as <span class=\"strong\">could</span>, <span class=\"strong\">might</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">would + have + the past participle</span> of the verb. This structure adds meaning to the main verb and can convey annoyance when you use them properly. Remember, when you talk about annoyance in the past, you use the <span class=\"strong\">modal + have + past participle</span>. </br></br>Take a look at the chart below. </br></br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span>  or <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express annoyance.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> can</span> be so insensitive.</br>Would that be asking too much?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present</br></br></br>     \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span>  or <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express annoyance when someone doesn't do something.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might</span>have let me know when she's going to fly to Africa for a week. <br/>You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could </span> at least think about other people's  feelings once.  </br></br> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have</span> , <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have</span>  or <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To make a critical comment.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have</span> told me about that guy in New York.<br/>He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have</span> offered to pay.<br/>I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have</span> said something different.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Could</span> you not be so judgmental all the time?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Must</span> you always talk like that?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\"> might have</span> let me know! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> that be too much to ask?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Notice that the meaning of those expressions depends on the right context and tone of voice.<br/> For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I took Carol out to dinner last night, because it was her birthday. I didn't tell her I got fired one week ago. She might have offered to pay.</span><br/> In this sentence, the speaker does not express annoyance; he is expressing a possibility.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "adorable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inspiring great affection; delightful; charming", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You two are adorable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spectacular", "type": "name"}, {"content": "beautiful in a dramatic and eye-catching way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going with her on her spectacular getaway to Africa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "getaway", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a vacation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going with her on her spectacular getaway to Africa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hold up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be forced to wait", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We don't want to be held up in traffic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to traipse", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to walk wearily or with reluctance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My girlfriend and I are traipsing off to Africa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "roll the dice", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to take a chance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ready to roll the dice just one more time?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss a time I said goodbye to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a story talking about when I said goodbye to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use contrast and comparison to describe how things have changed since they have been gone.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my story with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss a time when you had to say goodbye to a close friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What were the circumstances? What were your feelings?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 200-word story about about saying goodbye to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The story can be a personal account or it can be fictional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use vocabulary of contrast and comparison to talk about how things have changed since your friend left.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with a partner and ask for feedback.", "type": "text"}]}]}